      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburg%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1753, the area of present-day Hamburg was part of Newton Township when Sussex County was formed from Morris County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburg%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hamburg, New Jersey was once included within the boundaries of Vernon Township when it was formed from Hardyston Township in 1793.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamburg%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The boundary line changed in 1852, returning Hamburg to Hardyston Township before it became its own borough.",
